    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Another type of sychronization",
      "images": 6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Another type of sychronization",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 120.7,
          "cw": 18.35
        },
        {
          "text": "• Locks allow one type of synchronization between",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.258,
          "bottom": 0.326,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "threads – mutual exclusion",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.316,
          "bottom": 0.379,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.55
        },
        {
          "text": "• Another common requirement in multi-threaded",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.376,
          "bottom": 0.443,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "applications – waiting and signaling",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.434,
          "bottom": 0.496,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.93
        },
        {
          "text": "– E.g., Thread T1 wants to continue only after T2 has",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.493,
          "bottom": 0.552,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "finished some task",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.544,
          "bottom": 0.598,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.87
        },
        {
          "text": "• Can accomplish this by busy-waiting on some",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.595,
          "bottom": 0.663,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "variable, but inefficient",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.654,
          "bottom": 0.716,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.24
        },
        {
          "text": "• Need a new synchronization primitive: condition",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.713,
          "bottom": 0.781,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "variables",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.771,
          "bottom": 0.833,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.03
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Condition Variables",
      "images": 6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Condition Variables",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 222.5,
          "cw": 18.23
        },
        {
          "text": "• A condition variable (CV) is a queue that a",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.257,
          "bottom": 0.329,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "thread can put itself into when waiting on",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.319,
          "bottom": 0.386,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.93
        },
        {
          "text": "some condition",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.376,
          "bottom": 0.442,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 14.33
        },
        {
          "text": "• Another thread that makes the condition true",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.439,
          "bottom": 0.511,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "can signal the CV to wake up a waiting thread",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.501,
          "bottom": 0.568,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 13.09
        },
        {
          "text": "• Pthreads provides CV for user programs",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.565,
          "bottom": 0.637,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "– OS has a similar functionality of wait/signal for",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.634,
          "bottom": 0.697,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 15.55
        },
        {
          "text": "kernel threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.688,
          "bottom": 0.746,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 11.64
        },
        {
          "text": "• Signal wakes up one thread, signal broadcast",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.743,
          "bottom": 0.816,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 11.21
        },
        {
          "text": "wakes up all waiting threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.806,
          "bottom": 0.872,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 13.09
        }
      ]
    },
